{
  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
  "strings" : {
    "%lld of %lld photos saved" : {
      "comment" : "Burst card on the camera and VoiceOver after a burst with a Burst Limit: how many photos it saved of the photos one press asked for, such as 10 of 10 or 4 of 10. Draft wording for the Honesty review (issue #121).",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "%lld photos saved and signed." : {
      "comment" : "Shown after an exposure bracket: each frame was added to the photo library as its own photo, each with a Content Credentials signature. The number is the count of photos, at least 3. Honesty wording: says only that they were saved and signed.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A bracket never fires the flash." : {
      "comment" : "In Bracket Settings: the flash doesn't fire for any frame of an exposure bracket. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A photo can't be opened or shown correctly without these. They describe the camera's sensor and color, not you." : {
      "comment" : "Explains why the locked details are always saved. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release. Don't say these details can't identify a device or link photos: whether any value differs between two devices of the same model hasn't been checked. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "%lld optional details in the files" : {
      "comment" : "Summary line in the photo details: how many of the optional details (date, camera, lens and so on) the saved files hold. The location is not counted: it has its own line. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld optional detail in the files"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld optional details in the files"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld tags, blocks and properties in this file, as nope. read them back before saving it. Names are the standards' own." : {
      "comment" : "Top of a file's Every Tag page in the photo details: how many metadata items the file holds. Tag, block and property names are not translated. Keep nope. unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld tag, block or property in this file, as nope. read it back before saving it. Names are the standards' own."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld tags, blocks and properties in this file, as nope. read them back before saving it. Names are the standards' own."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A screen-size preview, not the full photo." : {
      "comment" : "Hint in the Last Photo viewer while the photo is zoomed in: what is shown is a screen-size preview held in memory, not the saved file. Honesty wording: must not claim more than the English. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A second photo, started %@ after nope.'s, with the processing iOS applies when an app asks for the highest quality. It may combine several frames, and it may differ from what other camera apps save." : {
      "comment" : "Compare view: what the phone-processed side is. The value is a time such as 850 ms. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "All Optional Removed" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row value: the master switch is on and no optional details are saved. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Always kept" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, next to a metadata item every file keeps because the photo can't be opened without it.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Always Saved" : {
      "comment" : "Section header above the details every photo keeps. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Analysis in Photos" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: the Photos app analyzes photos. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "App Name and Version" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: records that nope. made the file. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Apple encrypts and re-signs App Store apps, so there's no standard way to confirm a download was built from our public source." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 15 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. App Store is Apple's name. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Apple Watch Sends Only Commands" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: the Apple Watch app exchanges only commands and short status with the phone. Apple Watch is Apple's product name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "As written in the files." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Exposure and the Lens and Camera groups in the photo details: the values are exactly what the saved files hold. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Black and White Levels" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Camera Make and Model" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: which device took the photo. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Check It Yourself" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: how to verify that the app makes no connections. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Claim generator: %@ %@" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details: the software the Content Credentials manifest names as its claim generator. The values are a name and a version, such as Photivra Nope Camera 0.2.0.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Color Data and White Balance" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item: color matrices and the as-shot white balance. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Color Filter Pattern" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item: the sensor's red, green and blue pixel pattern. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Color Profile (HEIF and JPEG)" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item. HEIF and JPEG are file format names. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Content Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the photo details: the photo's Content Credentials signature. Content Credentials is the name of the C2PA standard's signatures. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Counted on the RAW sensor data when the photo was taken, over every photosite of the active area. Clipped highlights are within 0.5% of the white level or above it; clipped shadows are within 0.5% of the black level or below it, where 0.5% is of the range between the two levels." : {
      "comment" : "Footer in the photo details: how the RAW clipping is defined and measured. A photosite is one sensor element. The white and black levels are the RAW file's own values. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Custom" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row value: the person chose the optional details one by one. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Custom, Location On" : {
      "comment" : "Value of the Details in Each Photo row in Settings: the person chose the optional details one by one, and Location is on, so photos include where they were taken. A whole value; use the translations of Custom and Location On. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Date and Time Taken" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Details in Each Photo" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row and page title: which optional details (location, date, camera model and others) each photo includes. Replaces Choose Details and the Remove All Optional Details row. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Details in each photo: Location" : {
      "comment" : "Section header above the Location switch on Details in Each Photo (its own key: Location is also the switch's name).",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Location"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Details in This Photo" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the photo details: which metadata details the saved files hold and which they don't. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Developed by nope. from the RAW, Flat look" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, the processing of a HEIF or JPEG file: nope. developed it from the RAW with the Flat look (no contrast curve). Keep nope. unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Developed by nope. from the RAW, Standard look" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, the processing of a HEIF or JPEG file: nope. developed it from the RAW with the Standard look (one overall tone curve). Keep nope. unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Different" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the compare view's details, also spoken for each item: metadata both files hold, with different values.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Distortion correction: this lens doesn't let apps turn it off or report whether it's used, so its photos may be corrected for lens distortion." : {
      "comment" : "Processing note and photo details: the lens offers no switch for the camera's geometric distortion correction, which reshapes the picture. Keep \"may\": it isn't known whether the correction is applied. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Distortion correction: this lens lets apps turn it off, and nope. does." : {
      "comment" : "Processing note and photo details: the lens lets the app turn off the camera's geometric distortion correction, which reshapes the picture. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "DNG Version" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item. DNG is a file format name. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Each frame is a separate single-frame photo. Nothing is merged." : {
      "comment" : "Explains exposure bracketing. Must not claim more than the English: the photos are never combined.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Each frame is a separate single-frame photo. Nothing is merged. Stack them in other software." : {
      "comment" : "Explains focus bracketing in Bracket Settings. Must not claim more than the English: the photos are never combined by the app.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Each photo is one frame from the sensor, saved as RAW with as little processing as this phone allows. HEIF and JPEG copies are developed from it." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the format chip on the camera. RAW, HEIF and JPEG are file format names. Must not claim more than the English: as little processing as the phone allows, not zero. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release. On iPad the English names the iPad, and on other devices it says \"device\"; translate each variant. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "device" : {
              "ipad" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Each photo is one frame from the sensor, saved as RAW with as little processing as this iPad allows. HEIF and JPEG copies are developed from it."
                }
              },
              "iphone" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Each photo is one frame from the sensor, saved as RAW with as little processing as this phone allows. HEIF and JPEG copies are developed from it."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Each photo is one frame from the sensor, saved as RAW with as little processing as this device allows. HEIF and JPEG copies are developed from it."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each photo is separate. Nothing is combined. Keep nope. open while the series runs." : {
      "comment" : "Explains interval shooting. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
