    "Focus is a position on this lens’s own scale from 0 to 1, not a distance. Kept by nope. until it closes; not written to the files." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Bracket group in the photo details of a focus bracket's frame. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name. Must not claim more than the English: no distance is known, and the values are in memory only.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "HEIF with some device processing" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken format name for the no-RAW fallback. HEIF is a file format name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Hold the time since the device restarted and IDs for each photo, which can link your photos. Off: nothing visible changes." : {
      "comment" : "What maker notes contain, and what turning them off costs. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Honesty" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row and screen title: what nope. does and doesn't do, and what it can't control. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iCloud Photos" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading. Apple's feature name: use the name iOS shows in this language. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "If you opt in, Apple may share aggregated, non-identifying crash and usage statistics with developers. They never include your photos. It's in Settings › Privacy & Security › Analytics & Improvements." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 12 and note 12 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. Use the setting names iOS shows in this language. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Image Size and Layout" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item: image size, bit depth, compression and data layout. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "In Night Mode, shows the live picture in red too. Only the screen changes; photos keep their colors." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Red Viewfinder switch, which is always shown and takes effect in night mode. Night Mode is the name of nope.'s switch; use its translation. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "In Photos" : {
      "comment" : "Row in the photo details: how the files were added to the Photos app. Photos is the system photo library app. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "In the files" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details: the saved files hold this detail. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS Connections" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: iOS itself goes online. iOS is a product name. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS itself, for example iCloud Photos, makes its own connections." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 1 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. iOS and iCloud Photos are Apple's names. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS may detect faces in the viewfinder to decide where to focus. Focus on Faces in nope.'s settings decides only whether nope.'s autofocus and auto exposure follow them. nope. doesn't read or save which faces it found." : {
      "comment" : "Honesty statement under Faces and Autofocus. Claim 18 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md (AVCaptureDevice face-driven autofocus and auto exposure); issue #80. Focus on Faces is the name of nope.'s own switch; use its translation. Must not say that the switch turns face detection off. Must not claim more than the English. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS Version" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: the operating system version. iOS is a product name; keep it unchanged. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "JPEG with some device processing" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken format name for the no-RAW fallback. JPEG is a file format name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Keep Screen On" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: what the Keep Screen On switch does to the screen, the battery and locking. Keep Screen On is the name of nope.'s own switch; use its translation. Draft wording for the Honesty review (issue #97). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Keep Screen On stops the screen from locking by itself while the camera is showing, so the camera keeps running and uses more battery. The screen dims after the time chosen in Dim After without a touch, 2 minutes unless you change it. With Never it doesn't dim, which uses more battery and can warm the phone; it still dims after 30 seconds in Low Power Mode and when the phone is hot. After 30 minutes without a touch or a photo, the phone's Auto-Lock applies again. While the screen is on, the phone is unlocked. The side button always locks it." : {
      "comment" : "Issues #97 and #119; docs/design/keep-screen-on.md, wording 7, and docs/design/finish-1.0.md, 4.4. Keep Screen On, Dim After and Never are the names of nope.'s own switch, menu and choice; Low Power Mode and Auto-Lock are Apple's names: use the names iOS shows in this language. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "device" : {
              "ipad" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Keep Screen On stops the screen from locking by itself while the camera is showing, so the camera keeps running and uses more battery. The screen dims after the time chosen in Dim After without a touch, 2 minutes unless you change it. With Never it doesn't dim, which uses more battery and can warm the iPad; it still dims after 30 seconds in Low Power Mode and when the iPad is hot. After 30 minutes without a touch or a photo, the iPad's Auto-Lock applies again. While the screen is on, the iPad is unlocked. The top button always locks it."
                }
              },
              "iphone" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Keep Screen On stops the screen from locking by itself while the camera is showing, so the camera keeps running and uses more battery. The screen dims after the time chosen in Dim After without a touch, 2 minutes unless you change it. With Never it doesn't dim, which uses more battery and can warm the phone; it still dims after 30 seconds in Low Power Mode and when the phone is hot. After 30 minutes without a touch or a photo, the phone's Auto-Lock applies again. While the screen is on, the phone is unlocked. The side button always locks it."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Keep Screen On stops the screen from locking by itself while the camera is showing, so the camera keeps running and uses more battery. The screen dims after the time chosen in Dim After without a touch, 2 minutes unless you change it. With Never it doesn't dim, which uses more battery and can warm the device; it still dims after 30 seconds in Low Power Mode and when the device is hot. After 30 minutes without a touch or a photo, the device's Auto-Lock applies again. While the screen is on, the device is unlocked. Its lock button always locks it."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Kept by nope. until it closes, to group the frames here. Not written to the files; in Photos each frame is a separate photo." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Bracket group in the photo details. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name. Must not claim more than the English: the values are in memory only.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
