      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lenses Without RAW" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: on a lens that can't save RAW, the phone processes the photo. RAW is a file format name. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lets anyone check that the photo hasn't changed since it was signed. The signature names nope. and its version as the maker. It is not proof: anyone could make a file that says the same." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Sign Each Photo switch. No default note. Must not claim more than the English: the signature shows whether the file changed after signing; it names nope. and its version, but each file certifies its own key, so it doesn't prove that nope. made the file or who took the photo. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Live aids are measured on the preview, a few times a second, only while they show. Nothing is saved." : {
      "comment" : "Note under the focus peaking, histogram and live readout switches. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: where the photo was taken. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location access is off for nope., so photos can't include a location. To add one, allow location access in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under the Location switch when the person declined location access. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location access isn't allowed on this device, so photos can't include a location." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under the Location switch when a restriction, such as Screen Time, doesn't allow location access. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location is in the files" : {
      "comment" : "Summary line in the photo details: the saved files hold the location where the photo was taken (GPS). Shown with a warning symbol. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location is off unless you turn it on under Details in Each Photo in nope.'s settings. Then nope. uses your location only while the camera is open, and each photo gets its latitude and longitude, and its altitude when iOS reports one. A photo taken before iOS has a position, or from the Lock Screen, gets none. No direction, speed or GPS time is written, and nope. never sends your location anywhere." : {
      "comment" : "Issue #43; docs/PRIVACY.md, \"Location\". Honesty statement under Location Only If You Turn It On. Details in Each Photo is the name of nope.'s own settings page; use its translation. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release. \"nope. never sends\": iOS itself may contact Apple to find the position (see Finding Your Location). Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location is on, but location access is off, so photos are saved without a location." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation of the Location On chip when the person turned Location on but location access is off in the system settings. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location On" : {
      "comment" : "Warning chip on the camera: new photos include where they were taken.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location Only If You Turn It On" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: photos include a location only when the person turns Location on.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location stays off, because location access isn't allowed for nope. You can allow it in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Shown after applying a settings preset that includes Location when location access is off. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Locked" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver: this detail is always saved and can't be turned off. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Maker Notes" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: the camera maker's private notes in the file. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Manual Controls are on, so this choice is not used now." : {
      "comment" : "First row of the Fast Shutter page in Settings while nope.'s Manual Controls are on: the choice is kept, but not used until Manual Controls are off. Manual Controls is the name of nope.'s button; use its translation. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/SETTING-SCOPE.md). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Manifest SHA-256" : {
      "comment" : "Disclosure row in the photo details: opens the SHA-256 hash of the file's Content Credentials manifest, as 64 hexadecimal digits. SHA-256 is a standard name; keep it unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Manifest SHA-256, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Voice Control name of the Manifest SHA-256 row of one file in the photo details. The placeholder is the file's format, such as RAW (DNG). SHA-256 is a standard name; keep it unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Never uses more battery and can warm the phone. The screen still dims in Low Power Mode and when the phone is hot." : {
      "comment" : "Added to the note under the Dim After menu when Never is chosen. Never is the menu choice; Low Power Mode is Apple's name: use the name iOS shows in this language. The catalog has device variants (phone, iPad, device). \"Hot\" means the device's own heat warning level (serious), not the weather. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review (issue #119).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "device" : {
              "ipad" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Never uses more battery and can warm the iPad. The screen still dims in Low Power Mode and when the iPad is hot."
                }
              },
              "iphone" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Never uses more battery and can warm the phone. The screen still dims in Low Power Mode and when the phone is hot."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Never uses more battery and can warm the device. The screen still dims in Low Power Mode and when the device is hot."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "New photos include where they were taken: latitude, longitude and altitude. You can turn Location off under Details in Each Photo in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation of the Location On chip on the camera: new photos include their location. Details in Each Photo is the name of nope.'s own settings page; use its translation. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No contrast curve. nope. turns off noise reduction, sharpening and local tone mapping." : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, under a copy developed with the Flat look: what the look does. The same claims as the processing note. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No contrast curve: closest to the sensor, so it looks flat and low in contrast." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Flat look. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No Data Collected" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: the app collects no data. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No location in the files" : {
      "comment" : "Summary line in the photo details: the saved files hold no location. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No Network" : {
