      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No optional details in the files" : {
      "comment" : "Summary line in the photo details: the saved files hold none of the optional details (date, camera, lens and so on). Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No Preview" : {
      "comment" : "Title in the Last Photo viewer when the photo shown has no preview, so only its small thumbnail is shown: in the camera opened from the Lock Screen, which makes no previews, or when nope. couldn't make one. Honesty wording: must not claim more than the English. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "No RAW" : {
      "comment" : "Under a lens button: this lens can't save RAW. RAW is a file format name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. asks to add photos, never to read them. With that permission, iOS doesn't let nope. see or change what is in your library. The small pictures nope. shows of the photos you just took are kept in memory only, until nope. closes. So each time nope. opens, the Last Photo spot starts with a button that opens the Photos app." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 29 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md (PHAccessLevel.addOnly); docs/PRIVACY.md, \"Last photo and its details\"; docs/design/device-feedback-1.0.md, section 1. Last Photo is the name of the spot beside the shutter; Photos and iOS are Apple's names. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. contains no analytics, crash-reporting or advertising code, and collects no data." : {
      "comment" : "Claims 3 and 5 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md (Data Not Collected; privacy manifest). Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. contains no networking code and makes no network connections." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 1 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. couldn't make a preview of this photo. The photo is saved in Photos." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence under No Preview in the Last Photo viewer when nope. couldn't make a screen-size preview of the saved photo (the file couldn't be read for one), so only its small thumbnail is shown. Photos is the system photo library app. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged, lowercase with its period. Honesty wording: must not claim more than the English. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. didn't change this file's picture." : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, for a file the phone's camera processed (a lens without RAW): nope. didn't change its picture. Keep nope. unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. keeps previews in memory only and has released this one. The photo is saved in Photos." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence under Preview Not Kept in the Last Photo viewer. Photos is the system photo library app. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged, lowercase with its period. Honesty wording: must not claim more than the English. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. never connects to the internet and collects nothing about you." : {
      "comment" : "First-run statement 3 of 3. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release. \"Collects\" matches the Honesty heading No Data Collected: nope. keeps settings and presets on the device, but sends nothing. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. never writes this." : {
      "comment" : "Compare view, for a metadata item only the phone-processed version holds and that no nope. setting can turn on: nope.'s allowlist never writes it. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. on Apple Watch sends only your commands, such as the shutter and the delay, to nope. on your iPhone, and gets back only short status, such as \"Saved and signed\". No photos or photo details go to the watch. watchOS and iOS carry these messages between your paired devices in their own way; nope. opens no network connection." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 19 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md; issue #63. Apple Watch, iPhone, watchOS and iOS are Apple's names. \"Saved and signed\" is the watch app's own result text; use its translation. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Don't name a transport: Apple doesn't document how the system carries these messages. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope. takes single RAW frames one after another and saves each one as its own photo. It doesn't stack, merge or process them: stack them in other software." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the night sky (astro) helper. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name. Must not claim more than the English: the frames are never combined. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "nope.'s Content Credentials signature." : {
      "comment" : "Compare view: this item of nope.'s file is its Content Credentials signature. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not in the files" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, under a value the saved files don't hold: it is what the camera reported or the lens that was selected, kept by nope. in memory. Must stay true if those values stop being kept. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not measured: nope. can't read how this camera lays out its RAW samples." : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, why the RAW clipping isn't shown: the camera's RAW sample format isn't one nope. reads. Keep nope. unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not measured: the camera gave no RAW samples to count." : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, why the RAW clipping isn't shown: the camera returned no RAW sensor samples with the photo.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not measured: the camera's RAW file doesn't give black and white levels that nope. can apply." : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, why the RAW clipping isn't shown: the RAW file's black and white levels are missing or in a form nope. doesn't apply. Keep nope. unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not measured: the RAW samples and the RAW file differ in size." : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, why the RAW clipping isn't shown: the camera's RAW samples and its RAW file don't have the same size, so they can't be compared.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not measured: the RAW samples don't fit the RAW file's white level." : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, why the RAW clipping isn't shown: the camera's RAW sample values are larger than the RAW file's white level allows, so they can't be compared.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not saved: it is discarded when you close this view." : {
      "comment" : "Compare view: the phone-processed photo is never saved and is discarded on Done. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not saved: nope. couldn't confirm that the photo holds only the details you chose." : {
      "comment" : "Shown when a finished photo file contained a metadata detail that is not on the privacy list, or couldn't be checked, so the app saved nothing. Honesty and privacy wording. Keep the name nope. unchanged, lowercase with its period.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not Signed" : {
      "comment" : "Warning chip on the camera: photos are saved without a Content Credentials signature. Honesty wording: never imply photos are signed. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Not stored" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details: the RAW file holds no lens correction instructions.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Nothing more to this lens's file. HEIF and JPEG copies that nope. develops from a RAW get the Flat look: no contrast curve. For them, nope. turns off noise reduction, sharpening and local tone mapping." : {
      "comment" : "Processing note of a lens that can't save RAW, while the HEIF and JPEG look is Flat: nope. adds no processing to this lens's file, and what it does to copies developed from a RAW. HEIF, JPEG and RAW are file format names; Flat is the name of the look in Settings, use its translation. Must not claim more than the English. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
