    "When you share from Photos, location is included unless you turn it off under Options. Other details, such as the date and device model, may still be sent." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 14 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. Options is Apple's button name in the share sheet: use the name iOS shows in this language. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "While the camera is showing, the screen stays on for 30 minutes after your last touch or photo. Uses more battery. Not used while Battery Low shows." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Keep Screen On switch. Battery Low is the camera's warning; use its translation. Must not claim more than the English: after 30 minutes the phone's Auto-Lock applies again; when the screen dims is the Dim After menu below it. Draft wording for the Honesty review (issues #97 and #119).",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "With Compare on, nope. takes a second photo with the phone's processing, only to show it next to yours. That photo is never saved, signed or shared, and it is discarded when you close the comparison. Only your nope. photo goes to Photos." : {
      "comment" : "Issue #55; docs/PRIVACY.md, \"Comparison shot\". Compare is the name of nope.'s own camera switch; use its translation. Photos is the system photo library app. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. On iPad the English names the iPad, and on other devices it says \"device\"; translate each variant. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
